{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And as for you, you shall keep My covenant</b>. Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 17:9): the ו' (vav) adds to the first matter — 'As for Me, this is My covenant with you' — and you, be careful to keep it. And what is its observance? 'This is My covenant which you shall keep' — you of now — 'and your seed after you' — those yet to be born. And the Rav was correct in the plain sense. And they said (the Radak) regarding the reason for circumcision: that He set a memorial in the organ of desire, which abounds in turmoil and sin, so that they shall not engage with it except in what is commanded and what is permitted. And by way of truth, the meaning of 'this is My covenant with you' is like the meaning of 'Behold, I am with you' (Genesis 28:15), 'And He said, for I will be with you' (Exodus 3:12), 'May YHWH our Elohim be with us' (I Kings 8:57) — it says that the covenant will be with him and therefore he will be fruitful and multiply, and afterward He commanded that Abraham keep this covenant, and circumcision will be a sign of the covenant. Now, this sign is a sign like Shabbat, and therefore it would override it. And understand this (see Zohar, Lekh Lekha 89)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:50.782327814Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}